ent coefficient. The theory retains the Einstein gravitational action and introduces two unknown functions, V(φ) and L(φ).","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8137c3cb4737e37ab529674f4ab48271ef4999f3a5a2847b6e5962a73becb002","title":"How do the Gauss and spatial diffeomorphism constraints shape arbitrary-spin matter coupled to loop quantum gravity, and how far can this quantum kinematics be derived from classical higher-spin actions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:81354038ff3d5b31eccfbe453e32c48f2ad9e63ce60f4b3ba9ed25a14a75bac7","title":"Could an EDE potential with larger late curvature retain an early suppression of growth while weakening the scalar force? How would cosmological constraints change if only part of dark matter had an EDE-dependent mass?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0070"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:81bda0176ef136afdc69d14cce7021034a392b51b311857016ea140e5a168db1","title":"Can monodromy permit slowly evolving dark energy with a super-Planckian field value and a sub-Planckian axion period?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0072"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:81eabc4ff8e9fb4a26303a2c3a1492897c8b26b903fce62457950bc26c006592","title":"How can an anti-D3-brane multiplet description transform consistently under axio-dilaton modular transformations? The appendix treats τ and the background three-flux G3 as transforming objects and asks for compatible matter transformations and vector duality.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0072"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8157b3e136b460585752c19063dac2a821c3111d0a501ace198f7125d843ac62","title":"How does the higher-dimensional form-fiel